--TEST--
`$f(...)` on a `mixed` or `?callable` callee that is not a closure throws a catchable `LogicError` naming what it is — `rule:types/callable-values`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: lang:expressions/anonymous-functions
class Box
{
}

// A callee typed `mixed` is not proven a closure, so the call checks it when
// it runs. The class is `LogicError`, the one the same call throws for an
// argument of the wrong type.
array<mixed> $callees = ['strlen', 7, null, [1], new Box()];
foreach ($callees as mixed $callee) {
    try {
        echo $callee('x') as string, "\n";
    } catch (LogicError $e) {
        echo "caught: ", $e->message, "\n";
    }
}

// A `?callable` holding `null` is checked the same way.
?callable $none = null;
try {
    echo $none('x') as string, "\n";
} catch (LogicError $e) {
    echo "caught: ", $e->message, "\n";
}

// A closure behind a `mixed` is still called.
mixed $real = fn (string $s): string => $s . '!';
echo $real('x') as string, "\n";
--EXPECT--
caught: a value of type `string` cannot be called. Only an anonymous function or a method reference is a `callable`
caught: a value of type `int` cannot be called. Only an anonymous function or a method reference is a `callable`
caught: `null` cannot be called. Only an anonymous function or a method reference is a `callable`
caught: a value of type `array` cannot be called. Only an anonymous function or a method reference is a `callable`
caught: an object of class `Box` cannot be called. Only an anonymous function or a method reference is a `callable`
caught: `null` cannot be called. Only an anonymous function or a method reference is a `callable`
x!
